<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guntis Ulmanis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1939">1939</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guntis Ulmanis is a Latvian politician who was president of Latvia from 1993 to 1999, the first head of state after the restoration of independence. Elected by the fifth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saeima">Saeima</a> in July 1993, he oversaw the withdrawal of Russian troops in 1994 and Latvia's first steps towards Western institutions. He is a great-nephew of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karlis-ulmanis">Kārlis Ulmanis</a>, the interwar leader.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guntis-ulmanis.jpg" alt="Guntis Ulmanis" width="320" height="481" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Saeima · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flickr_-_Saeima_-_10.Saeimas_deput%C4%81ts_Guntis_Ulmanis.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
